---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { archivedDocuments } from '../data/documents';
import { KIND_LABELS } from '../data/schemas/documents';

/**
 * A deliberate gap page.
 *
 * Who holds office and how to reach each office are the two things residents
 * most often want, and they are exactly what this project cannot currently
 * source to its own standard. Saying so plainly, and saying where to look
 * instead, is more useful than a confident page that might be wrong.
 */

const officeDocuments = archivedDocuments.documents
  .filter((doc) => doc.kind === 'office-document' || doc.kind === 'citizens-charter')
  .sort((a, b) => (b.publishedYear ?? 0) - (a.publishedYear ?? 0) || a.title.localeCompare(b.title));

const latestOfficeYear = Math.max(...officeDocuments.map((doc) => doc.publishedYear ?? 0));
---

<Base
  title="Government"
  description="Who holds municipal office in Calatagan, and how to contact each office — what this project can and cannot yet verify, and why."
>
  <h1>Government</h1>

  <p class="notice">
    <strong>This page is deliberately incomplete.</strong> Two things residents most often need —
    who currently holds office, and how to reach each office — are the two things this project
    cannot yet establish to its own evidence standard. Rather than publish a plausible answer, it
    publishes the gap.
  </p>

  <h2>Elected officials</h2>

  <p>
    Calatagan elects a Mayor, a Vice Mayor and eight members of the Sangguniang Bayan. The May 2025
    local elections have been held and the results are a matter of public record.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>We do not publish the roster here</strong>, for one specific reason:
    <em>an election result is not proof of present incumbency.</em> Between an election and today, an
    officeholder can resign, be suspended, be disqualified, die, or be succeeded. Publishing
    election winners as current officials asserts something the election return does not say.
  </p>

  <p>What we would need to publish it:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      A Commission on Elections certificate of canvass or official published return, rather than
      media reporting of the count.
    </li>
    <li>
      A current roster from the Department of the Interior and Local Government or its municipal
      field office, confirming who is in office now.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Neither is currently reachable. COMELEC's published attachment directories return errors to this
    project's tooling, and DILG publishes no machine-readable municipal roster we have found.
    Election results are available from civic-tech derivatives of COMELEC data and from news
    organisations; both are useful for finding the answer and neither is sufficient to publish it.
  </p>
  <p class="src-note">
    This is tracked as an open item in <a href="/sources">Sources</a>. If you have a primary
    document, a correction with a citation is welcome.
  </p>

  <h2>Offices and contact details</h2>

  <p>
    A telephone number, an e-mail address and a postal address for the municipal hall circulate on a
    national government portal. We do not republish them as current, and the reason is worth stating
    precisely.
  </p>
  <p>
    Those contact details sit in a single record submitted by the LGU to that portal. Three other
    fields in the same record — the municipality's income classification, the name of its mayor, and
    its website address — are all demonstrably out of date. The income classification is two years
    stale; the website it lists no longer resolves at all. Contact details drawn from the same
    record, of the same vintage, cannot be presented as current simply because they are the only
    ones available.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Publishing a wrong phone number has a real cost.</strong> Someone travels to an office
    that has moved, or calls a line nobody answers, and concludes the information was checked when
    it was not.
  </p>

  <h2>What the archive holds</h2>

  <p>
    The municipality's former website published a set of {officeDocuments.length} documents naming
    individual offices, most of them in {latestOfficeYear}. They are listed below and are
    <strong>archived, not current</strong> — fees, requirements and processing times in a document
    of that age should be treated as a starting point for a question, not as an answer.
  </p>

  <div class="scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Document</th>
          <th scope="col">Kind</th>
          <th scope="col">Published</th>
          <th scope="col">Archived copy</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {officeDocuments.map((doc) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{doc.title}</th>
            <td>{KIND_LABELS[doc.kind]}</td>
            <td>{doc.publishedYear ?? '—'}</td>
            <td><a href={doc.archiveUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Open ↗</a></td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="src-note">
    These documents are named for an office; this project has not opened them, so it does not
    describe their contents. They appear in the full <a href="/documents">document index</a> with
    the rest of the archive.
  </p>

  <h2>If you need to reach the municipality today</h2>
  <p>
    Go in person to the municipal hall, or contact the Provincial Government of Batangas, which
    maintains current contact routes to its municipalities. This project would rather send you to a
    source that is current than to one of its own that might not be.
  </p>

  <style>
    .notice {
      background: var(--warn-bg); border: 1px solid var(--warn-line);
      border-radius: 4px; padding: 12px 14px;
    }
    .src-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; }
    th[scope='row'] { text-align: left; font-weight: 500; }
    li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  </style>
</Base>
